A||||6||WisconsinGT||What's up with this?||||1||
Z||000000||WisconsinGT||11-20-2000||12:06 AM||||I removed my 180 stat and put in the stock 195. Did that make a big difference on how my car runs. Purs like a kitten. Idle is smooth, (It was idling rough) no miss under steady throttle. How can this happen? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||mshill||11-20-2000||01:38 AM||||If your temp sensor is off a little, the computer may have thought that the engine wasn't warm and might have been in open loop mode.  Now with 195 stat in it pushes it over the top into what the computer thinks is the normal operating range.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||11-20-2000||05:04 PM||||If you put in a low temp stat, you also need to put in a lower temp fan switch. Could be the problem, setting an open loop mode.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||11-20-2000||06:25 PM||||The fan switch is totally independent of the thermostat.  I ran a 180 all summer without a problem.  I put in the 195 last week when the morning temps got down into the 40s so the car would warm up faster and not run too cold due to the outside temperature.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WisconsinGT||11-20-2000||11:07 PM||||Thanks guys! Where is the temp sensor?||||reg||1
Z||000005||ArchMagi||04-03-2001||01:31 AM||||This has probly been posted a million times but whats the normal operating temp and oil pressure.  <P>im running a 87 4cyl. <P>TIA!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||04-03-2001||09:29 AM||||The fan switch has nothing to do with the car running in open loop mode.  That has to do with the temperature the ECM is reading. The only way to change that is to change PROM chips.  A fan switch will only turn on the fan at a specifc temperature.  It doesn't communicate with the ECM in any way.||||reg||1
